## 2. Accuracy self-assessment: **~97%** (statutory content)

Every rate/rule is grounded in cited primary sources:
- **Social security (Ley 100 de 1993):** Salud 12.5% (EE 4% / ER 8.5%), Pensión 16% (EE 4% / ER 12%); IBC floor 1 SMMLV, ceiling 25 SMMLV (COP 43,772,625). — *Ley 100/1993, Ley 1122/2007, Ley 797/2003*
- **FSP:** EE-only 1% at ≥4 SMMLV, 1.2–2.0% above 16 SMMLV — *Art. 27 Ley 100 / Art. 8 Ley 797/2003*
- **ARL:** ER-only, 5 classes 0.522%–6.960% by CIIU — *Decreto-Ley 1295/1994, Decreto 1607/2002*
- **Parafiscales:** SENA 2%, ICBF 3%, Caja 4%; exoneration <10 SMMLV — *Art. 114-1 ET (Ley 1607/2012)*
- **Retención en la fuente:** Art. 383 progressive table, UVT 2026 = COP 52,374 (*DIAN Res. 000238/2025*), 25% renta exenta cap 790 UVT (Art. 206 num.10, Ley 2277/2022), 40% global cap (Art. 336)
- **Leave & prestaciones:** vacaciones 15 días (CST 186); sick pay split employer d1–2 / EPS d3+ at 66.67% (Decreto 780/2016, CST 227); maternity 18wk / paternity 2wk (CST 236/236A, Ley 1822/2017, Ley 2114/2021); prima (CST 306), cesantías (CST 249), intereses 12% (Ley 52/1975)
- **Payslip mandate:** Ley 1393/2010 Art. 32 + DIAN Nómina Electrónica Res. 000013/2021 (correctly noting the CST has no single formatted-payslip article)
- **Identifiers:** employer **NIT** (DIAN/RUT), employee **C.C./C.E.** — not Spain's NIF/CIF/DNI/NIE

The worked example (COP 18,000,000 base → net COP 15,221,235; withholding COP 2,250,765 computed via the actual Art. 383 depuration) is internally consistent. I deliberately used a ≥10 SMMLV earner so all employer-contribution lines populate positively, with the exoneration for <10 SMMLV documented in the notes.

